[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115220,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ceruminous adenoma is a benign neoplasm of the apocrine cerumen-producing glands of the external auditory canal (EAC).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115221,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8420/0 Ceruminous adenoma</p>\r\n<p>8420/0 Ceruminous pleomorphic adenoma</p>\r\n<p>8420/0 Ceruminous syringocystadenoma papilliferum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115222,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F00.Y &amp; XH7AL8 Other specified benign neoplasm of middle ear or respiratory system &amp; Ceruminous adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115223,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> ceruminoma; ceruminomata; adenoma ceruminalis; cylindroma; eccrine cylindroma; aural hidradenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115224,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ceruminous pleomorphic adenoma; ceruminous syringocystadenoma papilliferum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115225,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours arise from dermal ceruminous glands confined to the outer half of the EAC. Direct extension of pleomorphic adenoma from adjacent structures should be excluded {15104293; 21792797}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115226,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms include an outer EAC mass with intact tympanic membrane, conductive hearing loss, otorrhoea or discharge, and otalgia {6243462; 6300574; 14102073; 15104293}. Imaging identifies an EAC soft tissue&ndash;density mass and excludes direct extension from adjacent sites {16168591; 23351401}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115227,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ceruminous adenoma represents &lt;&nbsp;1% of all primary ear neoplasms {6243462; 6300574; 15104293}, with an equal sex distribution and a wide age range (12&ndash;85&nbsp;years), with a peak in the sixth decade of life {6243462; 6300574; 15104293}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115228,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115229,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115230,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ceruminous adenoma is a unilateral, polypoid, grey, skin-covered mass measuring 10&ndash;40&nbsp;mm {6243462; 6300574; 15104293}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:19:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115231,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 293,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Ceruminous adenomas are circumscribed and usually unencapsulated, and they lack invasion. Surface pagetoid-type extension, ulceration, and pseudoepitheliomatous hyperplasia {6402199} may be seen.</p>\r\n<p>They are predominantly glandular, often with cystic change, and extend into the surrounding stroma. Solid back-to-back glands and papillary patterns may be identified. The dual cell population (comprising inner/luminal epithelial cells and outer basal/myoepithelial cells) is bland, with low to moderate cellularity. Luminal cells are cuboidal to columnar, with ample eosinophilic cytoplasm, showing apical snouting (apocrine). Isolated tumour cells show cytoplasmic golden-yellow/brown pigment granules. Myoepithelial cells are often spindled with clear cytoplasm. Mitoses may be increased (to as many as 4&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>), especially around ulceration or previous trauma/biopsy. Atypical mitoses and comedonecrosis are absent. Concurrent cholesteatoma may occur.</p>\r\n<h5>Subtypes</h5>\r\n<p>Tumours with chondromyxoid stroma represent ceruminous pleomorphic adenoma {32443830}, often with metaplastic elements {2545327; 7517760; 10349387; 16398681; 18314029; 24908278}.</p>\r\n<p>Ceruminous syringocystadenoma papilliferum shows papillary projections lined by a dual cell population, with a variably dense stromal plasma cell infiltrate {15104293; 16168591; 28490727}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Neoplastic cells react strongly and diffusely with pancytokeratin; luminal cells express CK7, EMA, and KIT (CD117); basal cells express myoepithelial/basal cell markers {2545327; 15104293; 22623086}. GATA3 is usually positive in luminal or apocrine cells.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The most important differential is ceruminous adenocarcinoma. It is important to exclude direct extension of salivary gland tumours. Paraganglioma and middle ear neuroendocrine tumour (MeNET) are distinctive.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-16T15:44:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
